            <ArticleTitle>Time of onset of chest pain in acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>139-48</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the time of onset of chest pain in 1099 patients admitted to a coronary care unit with myocardial infarction using a statistical model. Statistical analysis demonstrated an excess of infarcts with time of onset of chest pain at 0700 hours (14%) and at midnight (11%), with the remaining infarct population (75%) forming a background distribution over the 24 hr.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
